    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n31551" root="غدو" body-key="g">
    
      <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">مَغْدًى</span></b>  and ↓ <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">مَغْدَاةٌ</span></b>  [<i>A place to which people go,</i>
or <i>to which they return, in the period of the morning called</i> <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">غُدْوَة</span>; opposed to <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">مَرَاحٌ</span> and <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">مَرَاحَةٌ</span>]. ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b2- 
[Hence] one says, <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">مَا تَرَكَ فُلَانٌ مِنْ أَبِيهِ مَغْدًى</span>
<span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">وَلَا مَرَاحًا</span>, and <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">وَلَا مَرَاحَةً</span> ↓ <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">مَغْدَاةً</span></b> , expl. in art.
<span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">روح</span>. (S in art. <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">روح</span>, and K in the present art.)

